Description: Open-source parametric 3D CAD for hobbyists
 HobbyCAD is a Linux-native parametric 3D solid modeler built on
 OpenCASCADE Technology (OCCT) and Qt 6.  It provides boundary
 representation (B-Rep) modeling with STEP, IGES, STL, and OBJ
 import/export, a tiered startup system that adapts to available
 GPU capabilities, and an embedded command-line terminal for
 scripting and batch operations.
 .
 HobbyCAD operates in three modes depending on the system:
 Full Mode (OpenGL 3.3+), Reduced Mode (no GPU required for
 file conversion and geometry operations), and Command-Line
 Mode (headless batch processing).

Package: libhobbycad-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
# The public headers include OpenCASCADE headers (TopoDS_Shape.hxx and
# TopoDS_Face.hxx from modeling-data; Standard_Failure.hxx,
# Standard_Version.hxx and Poly_Triangulation.hxx from foundation), and
# without Qt they include <nlohmann/json.hpp> as well. Without these a
# consumer installs headers it cannot compile: the include fails on
# TopoDS_Shape.hxx before anything of ours is reached. Only the two OCCT
# packages the HEADERS need are listed; the others in Build-Depends are
# for building the library itself.
Depends:
 libocct-foundation-dev,
 libocct-modeling-data-dev,
 nlohmann-json3-dev (>= 3.12.0),
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Development files for the HobbyCAD core library
 The static library and the public headers of libhobbycad, the Qt-free
 core behind HobbyCAD: geometry, sketch entities and constraints, the
 constraint solver, the document model, file I/O, units and parsing.
 Third-party tools and plugins build against this; the application
 package does not need it.
